{
  "description": "How Pery's answers, page translations and journal text are read as Markdown. The web engine (web/src/ui/Markdown.tsx) and the Mac app (PerydaKit Markdown.swift) must both produce exactly these blocks and spans. Block types: p (paragraph), h (heading), quote, ul, ol, hr (a line). Spans list only the styles that are on; neighbouring plain text is one span. Links and images keep only their words.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "name": "a typical answer: heading, star bullets, a line, numbers, a quote",
      "text": "### Kısaca\n\nBu cümle **iki** şey söylüyor:\n\n* Birincisi, *zaman*.\n* İkincisi, `mekân`.\n\n---\n\n1. Bir\n2) İki\n\n> Alıntı bir\n> devam\n\nSon paragraf\nikinci satır.",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "h", "text": "Kısaca" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "Bu cümle **iki** şey söylüyor:" },
        { "type": "ul", "items": ["Birincisi, *zaman*.", "İkincisi, `mekân`."] },
        { "type": "hr" },
        { "type": "ol", "items": ["Bir", "İki"] },
        { "type": "quote", "text": "Alıntı bir devam" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "Son paragraf ikinci satır." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "every way of writing a line",
      "text": "a\n\n***\n\nb\n\n___\n\n* * *\n\n- - -\n\n----------",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "a" },
        { "type": "hr" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "b" },
        { "type": "hr" },
        { "type": "hr" },
        { "type": "hr" },
        { "type": "hr" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a line of dashes or equals signs right under text makes that text a heading",
      "text": "Birinci bölüm\n---\nmetin\n\nİkinci\nbölüm\n===\n\n===",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "h", "text": "Birinci bölüm" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "metin" },
        { "type": "h", "text": "İkinci bölüm" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "===" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "heading levels, closing hashes, and hashes that are not headings",
      "text": "# Bir #\n###### Altı\n####### yedi\n#etiket",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "h", "text": "Bir" },
        { "type": "h", "text": "Altı" },
        { "type": "p", "text": "####### yedi #etiket" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an indented line continues a list item; nested items join the list",
      "text": "- bir\n  devamı\n  - alt\n- iki\n\nsonra",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "ul", "items": ["bir devamı", "alt", "iki"] },
        { "type": "p", "text": "sonra" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "other bullet marks, and lists of different kinds side by side",
      "text": "• bir\n+ iki\n1. üç\n- dört",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "ul", "items": ["bir", "iki"] },
        { "type": "ol", "items": ["üç"] },
        { "type": "ul", "items": ["dört"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "stars inside text are not bullets",
      "text": "2 * 3 * 4 eder\n*vurgu* ile başlayan satır",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "p", "text": "2 * 3 * 4 eder *vurgu* ile başlayan satır" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "Windows line ends",
      "text": "a\r\nb\r\n\r\n- c",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "a b" },
        { "type": "ul", "items": ["c"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "nothing",
      "text": " \n\n  ",
      "blocks": []
    }
  ],
  "inline": [
    {
